# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The root Dockerfile's build context is the PROJECT ROOT (see
# docker-compose.yml and render.yaml -- both build from `.`) so it can COPY
# both backend/ and frontend/ into one combined image (see the Dockerfile's
# own module comment for why it's one image/service now instead of three).
# Without this file, `docker build`/`docker compose build` would transmit
# EVERYTHING in the repo root to the Docker daemon as build context --
# including a real ".env" full of secrets, if one exists on disk, even
# though no COPY instruction ever references it. Excluding it here means
# it's never even sent over, not just "not copied into the final image".
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets -- never send these to the Docker daemon as build context ------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Git / editors / OS -------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Python (backend has its own Dockerfile/context; nothing here needs these
# but keep the build context lean regardless) ---------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# --- Logs / misc ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
node_modules/

# --- Docs not needed inside the image ------------------------------------------
README.md
